WEBVTT

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.010
Shibuya River.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.800
This is where Joshua wanted to go.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.560
The Composer is up ahead.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.350
The Composer...

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.360
...is CAT!

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.280
However you figure it,
CAT's gotta be pullin' the strings!

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.650
Enjoy every moment with all you've got!

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.490
Looks like Minamimoto knows
where the Composer is too.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.990
Yeah.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.120
I won't let 'im beat us there.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.830
I'll bring everyone back!

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.080
That's right.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.670
There's light.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.140
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.180
"#11: The Hour of Reckoning"

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.980
Minamimoto.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.730
We ain't got time for you!

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.400
Out of our way, Taboo Breath!

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.070
This is as far as you can go.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.160
Oh yeah?!

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.830
There's a barrier even I can't break.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.750
It's the Iron Maiden's handiwork.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.330
Is Konishi up ahead?

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.120
You hectopascal.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.210
She's not "up ahead," you zetta simpleton.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:58.010
--What?
--Where is she then?

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.590
Haven't you noticed?

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:02.760
What do you--

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.720
That's right: I've been
with you the whole time.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.140
What's wrong?

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.390
I heard a voice just now.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.450
I didn't anticipate I'd
be emerging like this.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.490
Y-You were hidin' in my damn shadow?!

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.160
You picked the wrong
place to put a barrier.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.170
I know this is your fault. Now, open it.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:34.790
Otherwise...

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:44.720
...I'll turn you into sludge
in the Shibuya River.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.850
Very well.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.190
I'll remove the barrier.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.520
However,

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:58.400
if you become the Composer, you will
appoint me to Kitaniji's position.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.650
That's my stipulation.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.280
Switching sides?

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.450
According to my analysis, Shibuya has
begun moving toward a full stop.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.750
There will be a major
upheaval in the near future.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.130
And the one with the best
odds of surviving the chaos

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.050
is a free spirit: you.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.220
Please Excuse My Dear Aunt Sally!

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.190
Sentiment and hesitation are trash!

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.940
I zetta dig your style! You've got a deal.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.480
In that case, I'll remove the barrier.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.360
Listen up!

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.820
All you zeroes in the Underground!

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.280
Your new Composer...

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:54.460
...is me!

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.550
Move!

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.680
This is as far as you go.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.600
I don't care who the Composer is,
as long as my authority is assured.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.930
You bitch.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.520
Rhyme!

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:21.480
You disruptive elements will
interfere with my predictions.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.860
I'll erase every last trace of you!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.040
Where...?!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.790
We're floating?!

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.540
Grab on!

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.050
What the...?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.390
Take this.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.820
What are you looking at?

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.700
Nothin' works on her!

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.080
Focus!

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.710
I don't think so.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.140
If this keeps up...

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.980
I'll act as a decoy and buy time.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.860
Focus while she's distracted and let her
have it with your strongest psych.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.650
If she gets me and I'm erased,

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.570
take Rhyme and--

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.030
No thanks.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.030
I'll get Rhyme back for sure,

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:57.540
but you're the only one who
can bring her back to life!

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.210
Let's do this, partner!

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.500
The next composer...

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.000
...is gonna be me!

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.880
Your flailing is pointless.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.970
Your defeat is within expectations.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:14.640
OK then, what exact time
am I gonna get taken out?

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.850
Go on, tell me!

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.060
Right now.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.370
How stubborn you are.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.950
Take this!

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.890
Know your place!

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.090
What?!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:56.680
Neku!

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.520
I'll take my time beating you...

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.810
...to death!

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.450
I was glad that you came to save me.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.910
I believe...

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.780
...in your idiocy.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.410
Let's get Rhyme back.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.710
And Shiki too!

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:40.890
Never... again!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.830
Beat?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:03.410
I made up my mind
not to let anyone else...

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:08.590
...die on my watch!

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:25.810
Rhyme?!

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:33.990
Now we've got Rhyme back,
we've as good as won!

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:37.030
I'll never let the likes
of you get your way!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.290
Focus, Neku!

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.210
<i>You're </i>telling me that?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.300
--Beat!
--Yeah. That's my sister for you!

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:03.140
Go!

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.030
Her weak point is her shadow!

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.240
Got it.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.570
Where...?

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:02.410
I can't see. Where are we?

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.370
Rhyme!

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.620
Sorry, sis, that was my bad.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:12.580
I won't let you go again!

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:18.090
My analysis...

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.760
...cannot be mistaken.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.220
Too bad, huh?

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:27.310
How could you summon Noise?!

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.600
You're not a Reaper!

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.270
'Cause I'm Rhyme's big bro!

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:37.690
A beautiful bond between siblings, then?

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:40.530
But... is it genuine?

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:41.740
Huh?

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.450
I'm the current Game Master.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:50.710
I know everything that was
taken from the Players.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:54.840
Your sister's memories
were your entry fee.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.040
Huh?

00:11:57.210 --> 00:12:01.430
Rhyme's memories... were <i>my </i>entry fee?

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:04.340
Beat, don't trust her.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:07.430
Your sister's entry fee
was something else,

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:11.940
meaning that her brother
doesn't matter to her.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:18.230
See? Your despair...

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:22.150
...is just... as I predicted.

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:32.500
Then, what... what was Rhyme's entry fee?

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.250
It must be her dreams.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.340
Shiki?!

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:47.850
Remember? Rhyme said she
didn't know about dreams.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:55.400
Shiki?

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:56.650
Is it really you?

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.230
But how...?

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:02.490
Well, when I woke up,
I could see your backs.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.400
Where is this place?

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.990
And is this...?

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.990
Neku! It's 'cause we beat Ironface!

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:15.250
The countdown is gone.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.000
We cleared the game!

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.750
So, we got our entry fees back?

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:21.960
Umm, what's going on?

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:24.630
I still look like this, so...

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.680
I think we're still in the Underground.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.810
It's my fault.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:32.600
You got taken as my entry fee.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.270
Huh?

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:35.100
What?!

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.940
I was your entry fee?!

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.980
Th-Then...

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.900
Wh-Why?!

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:44.820
Well, they take whatever
means the most to you.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.360
I'm sorry. I just...

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.740
I wanted you to come back to life.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:57.210
I wanted to see you smiling, walking
around Shibuya with your friends.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.760
You've changed, Neku.

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.300
Thanks to you.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.180
Umm...

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:15.060
But, I mean, I didn't do anything.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:18.940
W-We only got to see each other like
this because you two worked hard

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:21.320
and won the game for us.

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:25.280
No. That guy, Kitaniji,
isn't showing up like usual.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.610
What's that mean?

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.070
We haven't won yet?

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:30.280
Oh!

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.200
There's something there.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.330
Let's go look.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.180
Minamimoto.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.960
The final hour of reckoning is here.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.960
"The Room of Reckoning"

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:25.670
This is the Room of Reckoning.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.010
Kitaniji!

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.420
Where's the Composer?

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:35.310
The Composer is a noble being whose
first duty is to human happiness.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:38.930
He is on a different plane
from egoists like you.

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:40.690
So what?

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.940
I'm gonna become the Composer
and bring everybody back.

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:45.110
That's just it.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:50.450
That selfish desire is
the root of all suffering.

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:53.070
You're the same, Neku.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:57.120
You rejected interpersonal connections
and shut your ears, didn't you?

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.790
I thought it was the right thing to do.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:04.250
Individual desire becomes selfish egoism.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:06.800
That's what corrupted Shibuya.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:10.340
In order for Shibuya to be saved,
it must be reborn.

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:13.640
That is the true meaning
of this Reapers' Game.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:21.140
Shiki?!

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:23.310
Interference will not be tolerated.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.900
You bastard! What did you do to Shiki?!

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.530
To right the countless wrongs...

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.320
Shiki, are you OK?!

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.910
...of our day, we shine this light...

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.120
This ain't good.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.530
Shiki!

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:40.700
...of true redemption...

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.290
She's like the people
we saw around Shibuya.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.090
That this place...

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.380
...may become as paradise.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:55.510
What a wonderful world...

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:57.640
...such would be.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:23.870
Damn it!

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.040
Why?

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:30.750
Why are you doing this?!

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.220
Don't get distracted!

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:40.140
Stop!

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:41.600
Don't hurt Shiki!

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.430
Look closer, moron!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.560
That light!

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.900
Yeah. It's a pin.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.060
You mean...

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.280
Shades must've set it up.

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.570
If we got rid of that...

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:53.780
Watch out!

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:05.500
Did you imagine <i>that </i>would be enough
to defeat me or the Composer?!

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:28.020
Brace yourself.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.290
What?!

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.660
How about...

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.040
...this?!

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:08.690
Shiki!

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.820
It's all because of these pins.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.530
The Composer.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:20.950
Mr. Hanekoma.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:37.340
I made it this far because
everyone was there for me.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:40.260
I'll put an end to it all myself.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.510
It's not over yet.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:47.100
I will protect Shibuya!

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.440
That's...

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.480
Don't only Players have those?

00:19:56.980 --> 00:20:00.320
I'm running out of time.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:06.450
This world is like an orchestra.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:08.080
Huh?

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.540
Just as music requires
a skilled conductor,

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:15.290
if humanity were to unite under
a single leader, a single ideal,

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.840
it would reach a world of bliss.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.300
Your ideals are twisted.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:23.140
Negative emotions attract Noise, right?

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:27.510
You must have felt it in Shibuya too.

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:30.810
Anger. Hatred. Sorrow.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:34.230
Envy. Fear. Self-deprecation.

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:38.530
Countless selfish desires collide.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.280
They become unpleasant noise and amplify.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:44.530
They produce the wrongs of our day.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:49.240
If I strip it of individuality and
supply a shared idea in its place,

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:52.290
the world will become as paradise.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:55.080
The whole world, sharing one idea?

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.880
That's not...

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.800
I can make it possible
with the Red Skull pins!

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:02.760
You were behind those?!

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:06.010
I had them based on the
Composer's Player Pins!

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.180
All to conduct humanity to a new world!

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.810
To right the countless wrongs of our day,

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:15.770
we shine this light of true redemption,

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:18.980
that this place may become as paradise.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:22.740
What a wonderful world such would be.

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.150
No!

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.450
I was bad at dealing with people.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:29.450
I shut my ears to shut people out.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.500
But nothing changes when you do that.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.410
Your world won't grow!

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.790
You can't enjoy the moment!

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:45.130
Clashing with people in the
Underground taught me!

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.890
I was angry, worried, sad...

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:50.850
I don't need to stifle my feelings!

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:53.640
Having lots of emotions is good!

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:55.770
I knew it! It <i>is </i>you!

00:22:02.690 --> 00:22:05.360
Shibuya should stay...

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:06.660
...just the way it is!

00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:46.880
"It's a Wonderful World."
